+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+Measured on the adversarial synthetic vocabulary used by the bench harness: a
+Zipf-distributed store of 30 frequent domain words plus 2 000 rare identifiers
+(`crates/muninn-bench/src/main.rs`, `WORDS` / `word()`), which stresses term
+selection because a handful of terms appear in a large share of records.
+
+- **Before the fix:** full-recall p95 of the UserPromptSubmit hook was
+  **10.27 ms** on this adversarial 30-word vocabulary.
+- **Fix:** term selection now drops any candidate term whose document
+  frequency exceeds a third of the store (`df > n / 3`) before scoring by
+  IDF, since such a term carries no discriminative signal but still costs a
+  long FTS5 posting list to score. See `select_terms()` in
+  `crates/muninn-core/src/recall.rs`.
+- **After the fix:** full-recall p95 dropped to **1.82 ms** on the same
+  adversarial vocabulary.
+
+These figures come from a prior project benchmark run recorded in this
+project's own session history, not from a re-run performed while writing this
+document.
